/-! # Kernel proof of `Ix.Cert.RoleClosure.DefaultAdmits`

Proves every computational step of `Ix.Cert.RoleClosure.DefaultAdmits` unconditionally in Lean's
kernel in `< 30s` and `< 6 GiB` RSS (no extra axioms):
* relates `RoleData.table` (10,138 hex chars / 5,069 bytes) to `String.ofList (hexCharsOfBytes ...)`
  by `Eq.refl` and proves `bytesOfHex RoleData.table = some defaultRoleTable.toBytes` and
  `defaultTableBytesOf RoleData.table = .ok defaultRoleTable.toBytes` unconditionally via
  `bytesOfHex_ofList_hexChars`, avoiding quadratic `String.toByteArray` / `utf8GetAux` expansion;
* obtains `RoleTable.ofBytes` by canonical round-trip (`RoleTable.ofBytes_toBytes`) and discharges
  `RoleTable.check` via `firstRepeat_eq_none_of_nodup` so no `Std.HashSet` / `USize` evaluation is
  needed in the kernel;
* evaluates `Address.admissionHash` (`Blake3.Pure.digest`) through a strict `Nat`-word compression
  model (`compressN`, `chunkLoopCVN`, `treeRootCV5`) proved equivalent to `Blake3.Pure.compress`,
  proving `admitBinding_default` unconditionally;
* isolates the single 0-argument unfolding identity `DefaultTableBytesUnfolds`
  (`defaultTableBytes = defaultTableBytesOf RoleData.table`), which holds by `rfl` once
  `defaultTableBytes` delegates to `defaultTableBytesOf` instead of wrapping `RoleData.table`
  directly under `defaultTableBytes.match_1` (`ReducibilityHints.abbrev`). -/

